IO-03: give negative and NaN rainfall records no rain

A rain time series or a user-prepared rain file accepted any value as a
rainfall record, so a negative missing-data flag such as -1 became negative
rainfall and a "nan" made every result undefined. recordRate() now returns
no rain for a negative or NaN record, so nextNonzeroRecord() skips it like
an explicit zero, and a cumulative gage takes its increment from the last
valid record. The user-prepared rain file reader drops such values, as
legacy readStdLine() does with the 5.3.0 fix.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-03_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Gage.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Gage.cpp
index ce8b7a1..10a8434 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Gage.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Gage.cpp
@@ -219,11 +219,16 @@ double recordRate(const SimulationContext& ctx, int j, const Table& tbl, int k)
     const int rain_type = ctx.gages.rain_type[uj];
     const double interval = ctx.gages.interval_sec[uj];
     double r = tbl.y[uk];
+    // a negative or NaN record is not rainfall: it carries no rain
+    // (nextNonzeroRecord then skips it like an explicit zero)
+    if (!(r >= 0.0)) return 0.0;
     if (rain_type == 1 && interval > 0.0) {
         // one divide then one multiply (gage.c:692), not r/(interval/3600)
         r = r / interval * 3600.0;
     } else if (rain_type == 2 && interval > 0.0) {
-        const double prev = (k > 0) ? tbl.y[uk - 1] : 0.0;
+        int p = k - 1;                     // previous valid record
+        while (p >= 0 && !(tbl.y[static_cast<std::size_t>(p)] >= 0.0)) --p;
+        const double prev = (p >= 0) ? tbl.y[static_cast<std::size_t>(p)] : 0.0;
         r = (r < prev) ? (r / interval * 3600.0)
                        : ((r - prev) / interval * 3600.0);
     }
